<h2 id="section-2">2. How we use information</h2>
<p>We use personal information to:</p>
<ol>
<li>Provide the Service: create your account, build your roadmap, save your work, run the AI tools, HQ, its workflows, Ask 127, your AI team, site chat and Studio, the wins board and the Circle.</li>
<li>Process payments, apply taxes, send receipts and required billing notices (like renewal and price-change notices), and handle failed payments, refunds and chargebacks.</li>
<li>Send account and service messages, like email confirmation, password resets, receipts, renewal reminders, cancellation confirmations and important changes.</li>
<li>Send marketing emails and, if you opt in, texts. See Section 6.</li>
<li>Run the founding offer and referral program, including checking for referral abuse (for example, by comparing scrambled network identifiers).</li>
<li>Understand and improve 127: which resources help, where people get stuck, and how our tools perform. We may review AI conversations to fix problems, improve answers and enforce our Terms, with access limited to the people who need it.</li>
<li>Measure our advertising, only with your consent.</li>
<li>Keep 127 safe: prevent fraud and abuse, secure accounts, and enforce our Terms.</li>
<li>Comply with law, respond to lawful requests, and protect our rights and the rights of others.</li>
</ol>
<p>We don't use personal information to make decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects (like credit or employment decisions). Circle applications are decided by Eli. An AI summary may help him review them, but it never makes the decision.</p>
<h2 id="section-3">3. Eli's Playbook, the Idea Test and other AI tools</h2>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>What we send.</strong> When you use an AI tool, we send what you type, plus helpful context from your account (such as your stage, goal, obstacles, time and budget answers, 12-month goal, and roadmap progress), to our AI provider, <strong>Anthropic, PBC</strong>, to generate a response. Ideas you enter in the free Idea Test are sent the same way, and so is what an HQ workflow step, Ask 127, your AI team or your site chat needs when it uses AI (Sections 7B and 7C).</li>
<li><strong>How our AI provider handles it.</strong> Anthropic processes this information to provide the service to us. Under its commercial terms, Anthropic doesn't train its models on the content we send through our business account. It keeps API inputs and outputs for up to 30 days, longer only for content flagged for a possible breach of its usage policies (up to 2 years) or where the law requires.</li>
<li><strong>What we keep.</strong> We keep your most recent Playbook conversation (up to the last 40 messages) and your last 30 AI tool results in your account so you can come back to them. You can clear your Playbook conversation anytime with &quot;New conversation.&quot; Everything is deleted when you delete your account.</li>
<li><strong>Challenge summaries.</strong> If you tick the box to be featured in the Day One Challenge, we may use AI to summarize your check-in answers so Eli can prepare the live debrief. Check-ins from people who didn't tick the box aren't used for this.</li>
<li><strong>It's an AI.</strong> Responses are generated by AI, not written by Eli, and they can be wrong. Check facts in an AI response yourself before relying on them. See our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Be careful what you share.</strong> Don't put passwords, card numbers, government IDs, health information, or other people's private information into AI tools, beyond what an HQ workflow asks for.</li>
</ul>
