<p><strong>Advertising partners (only with your consent).</strong> If you accept advertising cookies, Meta and TikTok receive information about your visit and sign-ups through their pixels, and Meta may receive a hashed version of your email and first name when you submit a form. They use it to measure and improve our ads, and they may also use it under their own privacy policies, including to personalize ads. Some state laws call this &quot;selling,&quot; &quot;sharing&quot; or &quot;targeted advertising.&quot; You can refuse or withdraw consent anytime (see Section 5).</p>
<p><strong>Other members.</strong> Your first name and posts on the wins board are visible to other logged-in members. In the Circle, members see each other's names, what they share on calls and in the private group, and call notes.</p>
<p><strong>If you choose to be featured.</strong> If you tick the box on a Day One Challenge check-in, Eli may read your first name and the answers you chose on a public Instagram Live, in its saved replay, and in 127's Instagram stories and short clips. Anyone can see those, and Instagram handles them under its own policies. You can change your mind before the live by emailing us; after it airs, we stop using it in new posts but can't recall what was already shared.</p>
<p><strong>AI apps you connect.</strong> If you add your HQ AI link to an AI app such as Claude or ChatGPT, we share the information Sections 7A, 7B and 7C list with the company behind that app whenever the app asks for it, because you told us to. That company handles it under its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
<p><strong>Accounts you connect to HQ.</strong> When you connect an account (like Stripe, Shopify, Notion, an ad account, or your own account with a Studio company like Higgsfield), we read from it, send it what you ask HQ to, and write to it when you OK it, on your behalf. Those companies work for you under your own terms with them, and what they do with your data is up to their policies and your settings there.</p>
<p><strong>Business search (First 25 and HQ workflows).</strong> First 25, and HQ workflows that find businesses (like the gym video pack), find them through OpenStreetMap: Tracestrack finds the businesses and LocationIQ finds the city. We send these services only the business type and city you search for, from our server, not your name or email. Your list also holds public information about each business, from OpenStreetMap and from the business's own website, which we read once.</p>
<p><strong>Your referrer.</strong> If you join through a member's referral link and confirm your email, we tell that member someone joined with their link, and we may include your first name.</p>
<p><strong>Legal and safety.</strong> We may disclose information if required by law or legal process, or if we believe in good faith that it's needed to protect the rights, property or safety of 127, our members or others, or to investigate fraud or abuse.</p>
<p><strong>Business transfers.</strong> If 127 is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing or sale of assets, information may transfer as part of that deal, subject to this Policy.</p>
<p><strong>With your permission.</strong> For example, if you sign a testimonial release, we'll share what you agreed to.</p>
<h2 id="section-5">5. Cookies, pixels and your ad choices</h2>
<p>We use a small number of cookies and browser storage items that the Service needs to work, plus cookieless analytics. <strong>Advertising pixels (Meta and TikTok) load only after you click &quot;Accept&quot; in our cookie banner.</strong> They never run inside the member app.</p>
<ul class="bul">
<li>You can change your choice anytime with <strong>&quot;Cookie settings&quot;</strong> in the site footer.</li>
<li><strong>Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track:</strong> if your browser sends either signal, we treat it as a &quot;no&quot; to advertising cookies and pixels for that browser, and we don't ask again.</li>
<li>You can also adjust ad settings in your Meta and TikTok accounts.</li>
</ul>
<p>The full list of cookies and storage items is in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Notice</a>.</p>
<h2 id="section-6">6. Emails and texts</h2>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>Account emails</strong> (confirmation, receipts, renewal and billing notices, cancellation confirmations, security alerts) are part of the Service and go to everyone with an account.</li>
<li><strong>HQ's Monday check-in</strong> goes only to members who turn it on, until they turn it off (Section 7A). It's a service email, so it comes even if you've opted out of marketing emails, and it never includes offers.</li>
<li><strong>Marketing emails</strong> (founder emails, the weekly digest, launch news, offers) go only to people who opt in. Unsubscribe with the link in any email or in <strong>Settings</strong>. We process unsubscribes promptly, within 10 business days at most.</li>
<li><strong>Text messages:</strong> if we offer texts and you opt in, you can reply STOP to any text to stop.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="section-7">7. Recorded calls, Founder's Circle calls and gatherings</h2>
<p><strong>Founding members' call.</strong> The founding members' call with Eli (December 1, 2026) is recorded and the recording is shared only with founding members in the Library. You can keep your camera and microphone off and ask questions in the chat if you'd rather not appear in it.</p>
<p><strong>Founding Five.</strong> We use your application and hello video only to pick the five. At the start of each session we ask whether we can record it on Zoom, and whether an AI note-taker (currently Granola) can transcribe it for your recap. We do each only if everyone in the session says yes, out loud, and you can say no any week. You can also ask to go off the record anytime. Transcripts are seen only by the people at 127 who prepare the recap, recordings stay on Eli's computer, and both are deleted 90 days after each session. Recaps go only to the five. We use a clip, video or story of you in our posts, emails or website only after you OK that piece, and in a paid ad only if you say yes to that ad, and each one says you got four group sessions with Eli for sharing your build. You can ask us to stop using a piece anytime: we'll stop using it in anything new and take it down from our own accounts, website and emails within 7 days.</p>
<p><strong>Founder's Circle.</strong> Circle calls are transcribed by an AI note-taker (currently Granola) to prepare a written recap. We don't keep video or audio recordings, and the optional open table after the call and anything said off the record aren't transcribed. We announce the note-taker at the start of every call. Transcripts are seen only by the people at 127 who prepare the recap and are deleted after 90 days; recaps are shared only with current Circle members and kept while the Circle runs. We don't use them in marketing without the written permission of everyone identifiable. Gatherings aren't recorded, and we ask before using identifiable photos of you in marketing. See the <a href="/circle-agreement">Founder's Circle Member Agreement</a>.</p>
<h2 id="7a-hq-and-connected-accounts">7A. HQ and connected accounts</h2>
<p>HQ is the optional workspace where Builder and Founder's Circle members track and run their business.</p>
<p><strong>What HQ keeps.</strong> The numbers you type in or your connections send, week by week (posts, outreach, reach, visits, leads, replies, sales, revenue and up to 6 numbers you name), plus your North Number, targets, weekly calls and notes, and your latest Read my week feedback. We keep the most recent 104 weeks.</p>
<p><strong>HQ's tools.</strong> Tools like the Conversion tracker, Profit and break-even and Cash runway keep what you enter in them, such as funnel counts, prices and costs, and the cash you expect in and out, to work out your results. They don't use AI: we don't send what you enter to our AI provider or share it through your AI link. You can export a tool's entries as a CSV anytime, and Start over deletes them.</p>
