<p><strong>Your customers' details.</strong> For your weekly totals, we read your customers' details only in memory and discard them as soon as the totals are calculated; they never go into our database or our logs. When you run a workflow that needs order or customer details (like a note to last month's buyers), that run holds what it used for 180 days, as Section 7B explains, and our AI provider gets names and the facts the task needs, never email addresses or phone numbers. Please send only numbers to your 127 link.</p>
<p><strong>Your customers' information stays yours.</strong> When it passes through HQ, we handle it on your behalf and only to provide HQ to you: your totals and the workflows you run. We don't sell or share it, contact your customers on our own, use it for advertising or to train AI models, or combine it with other information. If you bought from a business that uses 127 and have a question about your information, ask that business: we keep its customers' details only in the workflow runs it starts and the leads it saves (Section 7B).</p>
<p><strong>Who sees your HQ.</strong> Your HQ is private to you. We don't show it to other members or use it in marketing. People at 127 look at a member's HQ only to help when you ask, to fix a problem, or to enforce our Terms. We record when you use HQ (for example, that you saved a week or connected Stripe), never your amounts, and we measure HQ use with counts, such as how many members logged a week.</p>
<p><strong>Read my week.</strong> AI writes only two parts of Read my week, and only when they appear. For written feedback from Eli's Playbook, we send our AI provider your last 12 weeks of HQ numbers, your weekly calls and your notes, as Section 3 describes. For a &quot;What stood out&quot; line, we send only this week's and last week's activity counts (messages sent, replies, calls booked and yeses, by type of business and time of day), never your sales or revenue, or your leads' names, contact details or messages. Your customers' details from Stripe or Shopify are never part of either. The rest of Read my week is counted on our servers, without AI.</p>
<p><strong>Screenshots.</strong> If you use Fill it in for me, we send your screenshots to our AI provider once to read the totals, as Section 3 describes. We don't save the images or write them to our logs. Until you check the numbers and press Save week, we hold only what it read (the totals, the week they cover, the app it saw, like &quot;Stripe dashboard&quot;, and short notes), for no more than 24 hours; once you save, they're part of your HQ numbers. Screenshots can show other people's details, so if you can, crop out customer names and contact details first. We tell the AI to report totals only, never anyone's personal details.</p>
<p><strong>Monday check-ins.</strong> If you turn them on, we email you each Monday with last week's North Number, up to 3 more numbers and where your week leaks, plus a link to log the week. Our email provider sends it, so it carries those numbers. The link works without a login, for that week only, for 15 days, so anyone you forward the email to could see and change that week's numbers. Turn check-ins off from the link in any check-in email or in HQ.</p>
<p><strong>Your AI link.</strong> If you make an AI link and add it to an AI app, the app can read, whenever it asks:</p>
<ul class="bul">
<li>your first name and plan;</li>
<li>your assessment choices (stage, business type, 90-day goal, biggest obstacles, weekly time, budget, channels, comfort with AI, how you learn best and interest in the Circle), your roadmap progress and next step, and your milestones;</li>
<li>if you're in the Founder's Circle, what you're building, your Build Target, your North Number and your commitments from your last call;</li>
<li>up to 12 weeks of HQ numbers, with your targets, weekly calls and notes, and whether your connections and Monday check-ins are on;</li>
<li>if your plan includes them, passages from your Brain, your house rules, decisions and notes, your skills and your activity log;</li>
<li>the playbooks your plan includes.</li>
</ul>
<p>It can also log numbers, notes and decisions you tell it, run your skills, and work with HQ's workflows and Pipeline as Section 7B explains. Sends, posts and changes in your accounts that it gets ready wait for your OK in HQ. It never gets your email address, password, payment details or keys, or other members' information, and it sees customer details from your Stripe or Shopify sales only where a workflow you ran used them or you saved them as leads (Section 7B).</p>
<p>You set up that sharing, so the app's company (for example, Anthropic for Claude or OpenAI for ChatGPT) handles what it reads under your account's terms with that company, its privacy policy and your settings there, including how long it keeps your chats and whether it uses them to train its models. That's different from Section 3, where Anthropic works for us under our business terms and doesn't train on your content.</p>
<p><strong>Keys and sign-ins.</strong> Keys, tokens and sign-ins you give us are encrypted (AES-256), never shown again after you save them, and never written to our logs. We use each only for what its card in HQ lists, even where it would allow more. HQ changes something in an account only when you tap OK in HQ for that change, and it never moves money out of your accounts, except a refund to your own customer that you OK. If we believe a key you gave us may have been exposed, we'll tell you promptly so you can replace it.</p>
<p><strong>Disconnecting and deleting.</strong></p>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>Disconnect</strong> a connection in HQ, under Connections, and we delete its saved key or sign-in right away (for Shopify, also your store address and the order ID numbers). The numbers already counted and the docs you imported stay until you delete them. Delete the key in that service too, or remove 127's access in its settings.</li>
<li><strong>Turn off or replace your 127 link</strong>, and the old link stops working at once. Turning it off also disconnects Shopify, which sends to it.</li>
<li><strong>Turn off or replace your AI link</strong>, and the old link stops working at once. What your AI app already read stays in your chats there until you delete them in the app.</li>
<li><strong>If your paid plan ends</strong> (a pause doesn't count), your 127 link and AI link stop working, Monday check-ins stop, and we delete your saved keys and sign-ins 30 days later. Your numbers stay with your account in case you come back.</li>
<li><strong>Delete your account</strong>, and everything HQ keeps is deleted with it.</li>
<li><strong>To delete your HQ numbers but keep your account,</strong> email us (Section 8).</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="7b-hq-workflows-and-your-clients-information">7B. HQ workflows and your clients' information</h2>
<p>HQ's workflows plan your work, write drafts and make files for your business, and its Pipeline keeps your leads and clients. Much of what's in them is about other people: your clients and leads, the contacts you import, docs in your Brain, what your connections bring in and chats on your site. Here's what we keep and how we handle it.</p>
<p><strong>What HQ keeps.</strong></p>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>Runs:</strong> what you enter to start a workflow (like a client's first name, a household's size or contacts you paste in), what each step made (plans, drafts, lists and files) and a log of the run.</li>
<li><strong>Your Pipeline:</strong> each lead or client you add or a workflow finds, with their name and business, the ways to reach them you save (email, phone, Instagram, website), your notes, the drafts for them, what they replied and the stage they're at.</li>
<li><strong>Your Library, repeats and Inbox:</strong> files you upload (like a contacts export) and files your workflows save (like a plan to print); the answers a repeat reuses, including a repeat you save as a skill; and Inbox cards, which hold a title and a short note.</li>
<li><strong>Your business details:</strong> what HQ knows about your business to fill in workflows and your emails (like your offer, price, area and mailing address), and small facts a workflow saves for next time (like which dishes a client had last week).</li>
<li><strong>Wins you log:</strong> what happened, a short note, the lead it was about, and who you let see it.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Your clients' information stays yours.</strong> We handle what you keep about your clients and leads as your service provider: only on your behalf and only to provide HQ to you (<a href="/terms#13c-hq-workflows-and-your-clients-information">Terms Section 13C</a>). We never contact them on our own. HQ writes drafts, and you send each one yourself, or, where you've connected an account that can send, HQ sends it from your account when you tap OK. The one exception is your site chat, which answers people who write to it on your website (Section 7C). We don't sell or share their information, use it for advertising or to train AI models, or combine it with information from other members. If you're the client or lead of a business that uses 127, that business decides what it keeps about you, so ask it first. If you write to us, we'll pass your request to that business.</p>
<p><strong>Who sees it.</strong> It's private to you. We have no screen that shows a member's runs, Pipeline or Library, and people at 127 look at them only to help when you ask, to fix a problem or to enforce our Terms. For example, if we review an account's age, we see the words that started the review, which can include what was typed into a workflow. A win you let us share reaches our team with the name you chose. Leave your client's name out of it: we never publish your clients' names or details.</p>
<p><strong>What goes to our AI provider.</strong> When a workflow step uses AI, or Do my day, call prep or Monday's card writes a draft, we send Anthropic what that step needs, as Section 3 describes. For a lead, that's usually their name, business, public links and what a workflow noted about them, your note, their last reply and their stage. Do my day, call prep and Monday's card leave out the email addresses and phone numbers you save. A workflow that reads images you add, like screenshots, sends those too.</p>
<p><strong>Health details in two workflows.</strong> The personal training workflow keeps only whether a client's PAR-Q+ says Go, Hold or Not done yet, the date they filled it in and when to redo it. It starts in HQ only, and the result stays out of your Pipeline, your AI link and our AI provider. The meal prep workflow keeps foods to leave out of a client's meals, which can include allergies, without saying which, and plans the menu without AI. Keep full health forms and allergy details in your own records.</p>
<p><strong>Your AI link.</strong> If you add your AI link to an AI app, the app can also list and start your workflows (except ones that start in HQ only), read a run's progress, drafts and results, read and answer your Inbox, and read and move the leads in your Pipeline (their name, business and stage, and the start of your note). Your files stay behind your HQ login. What the app reads, including your clients' and leads' details, goes to the app's company, as Section 7A explains.</p>
<p><strong>How long we keep it, and deleting it.</strong></p>
<ul class="bul">
<li>A run is deleted 180 days after it ends, with its Inbox cards. <strong>Delete this run</strong> deletes it sooner, with the files it saved, but not what it added to your Pipeline or a repeat's copy of its answers.</li>
<li><strong>Delete this lead</strong> deletes a lead from your Pipeline: its details, notes, drafts, the reply it sent and its history, plus the drafts and answers HQ wrote for it (with any reply you pasted) and what workflows saved under its name. Its name comes off your wins. Runs you started from a workflow's page, like a list of businesses, keep their results until you delete those runs.</li>
<li>Delete files in your Library, repeats and wins in HQ anytime.</li>
<li>For anything else, email us (Section 8). We'll do it promptly.</li>
<li>If your paid plan ends, your HQ work stays with your account in case you come back. Repeats stop running but stay saved.</li>
<li>Delete your account, and all of it is deleted.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="7c-your-brain-ask-127-ai-team-site-chat-and-studio">7C. Your Brain, Ask 127, AI team, site chat and Studio</h2>
<p>Where your plan includes them, HQ keeps your business's documents and rules, answers and acts for you in chat, runs AI helpers, answers visitors on your website and makes media. Here's what each keeps and where it goes.</p>
<p><strong>Your Brain.</strong> Docs you upload or type (like PDFs, Word files, spreadsheets and notes), pages you bring in from Notion or an Obsidian vault, your house rules (your principles, voice and how you do things), decisions and numbers you log, and facts HQ saves for next time. We keep each doc's text, not the file you uploaded, plus an index on our own servers that HQ uses to find the right passages. From an Obsidian vault we keep the notes' text, tags and links, not its other files. If a doc shows a full card or Social Security number, we keep only its last 4 digits.</p>
<p><strong>What goes to our AI provider.</strong> When a workflow, Ask 127 or a helper needs your Brain, we send Anthropic the passages that fit the task, never your whole Brain, as Section 3 describes. Your house rules go with every AI request HQ makes for you. Your docs can hold other people's information, and we handle it as Section 7B describes.</p>
<p><strong>Ask 127 and your AI team.</strong> We keep your chats with Ask 127 and what your helpers did. With each message, we send Anthropic your recent chat, your profile and house rules, the Brain passages that fit, your logged numbers, the titles of your recent runs and Inbox cards, and how many leads you have at each stage, without their names. When Ask 127 makes a plan for you, we also send Anthropic the titles of the 127 workflows, prompts, templates and other library items that fit what you asked, and the names of the apps you've connected or could connect, without anything from inside them. A step that uses an app's data reads it when it runs, as Section 7A describes. A workflow or helper sends what its task needs, as Section 7B describes, leaving out email addresses and phone numbers. Ask 127 suggests actions and takes each one when you tap OK. Anything they'd send, post, publish, charge, spend, delete or change in an account you've connected waits for your OK in HQ.</p>
<p><strong>Talking to HQ.</strong> When you tap Talk in HQ, your browser's own speech service turns what you say into text and reads HQ's answer aloud. Your browser may do this on its maker's servers (Chrome usually sends your voice to Google), and that company handles it under its own terms and privacy policy. We never get the recording, only the text, and we handle that like anything you type.</p>
<p><strong>Your activity log.</strong> HQ records what you approved, and what Ask 127, your AI team, your schedules, your AI link and your connections did: who or what acted, when, in which account and on which record. For your AI link, it records which tool was used, not what was sent. It doesn't copy the messages, docs or contact details themselves, so a lead you delete shows as deleted.</p>
<p><strong>Your site chat.</strong> If you add it to your website, it saves your visitors' messages and its answers for you, with the page they wrote from and any contact details they choose to leave for a reply (those also go to your Pipeline). It answers only from the docs and business details you mark public. We run it for you as your service provider: the chats are yours, we send them to Anthropic only to write the answers, and we don't use them for anything else or combine them with other members' information. If you chatted on a business's website and have a question about your chat, ask that business; if you write to us, we'll pass your request on.</p>
<p><strong>Studio.</strong> When you make images, video or voice, or captions from a recording, we send your prompt and the photos, video, audio or script you add to the company that makes it (Section 4 names them), get the result back and save it in your Library. Through 127's account, each works for us under our contract with it, as Section 4 describes, and doesn't train its models on what you send. If you connect your own account with one of them, it works for you under your own terms with it, including what it does with what you send (Section 4). If you make a voice or a look that copies you, the company makes it from the recordings or photos you add, and we keep it so you can use it again. Deleting it removes it from HQ and from that company. It's also deleted with your account, or 30 days after your paid plan ends.</p>
<p><strong>Back office.</strong> If you import bank or Stripe statements, we keep each line's date, description, amount and category, and hide full account and card numbers except the last 4 digits. We send Anthropic the lines it needs to suggest categories. Invoices and payment links are made in your own Stripe account when you OK them; we keep their number, amount and status, and your clients' card details stay with Stripe.</p>
<p><strong>Ads desk.</strong> If you connect an ad account (Meta, Google Ads or TikTok), we read your campaigns, ads and their results, like spend, clicks and cost per result. These are totals: ad platforms don't tell us who saw your ads. When you OK it, HQ creates paused ads and makes the changes you approve. We use your ad account's data only for you, never for another member or pooled into benchmarks. HQ doesn't upload your customer lists or send your customers' activity to ad platforms.</p>
<p><strong>How long we keep it, and deleting it.</strong></p>
<ul class="bul">
<li>Brain docs, house rules, decisions and saved facts: until you delete them or your account. <strong>Delete this doc</strong> deletes its text and index entries, and <strong>Delete my Brain docs</strong> deletes them all. A run that used a passage keeps its copy until the run is deleted (Section 7B).</li>
<li>Ask 127 chats: your last 60 messages, until you start a fresh chat, and never more than 180 days after the last one.</li>
<li>Your activity log: 400 days, then deleted.</li>
<li>Site chats: 180 days after the chat, or sooner if you delete them.</li>
<li>Files in your Library, like Studio results, filled templates, tools and site files, and imported statements you save: until you delete them or your account, even after a paid plan ends.</li>
<li>Bookkeeping entries: until you delete them or your account.</li>
<li>Ad results HQ keeps: until you disconnect the ad account or delete your account.</li>
<li>A voice or look that copies you: until you delete it or your account, or 30 days after your paid plan ends.</li>
<li>Delete your account, and all of it is deleted.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="7d-rules-from-the-platforms-you-connect">7D. Rules from the platforms you connect</h2>
<p>When you connect an account by signing in, that platform's rules for apps like HQ also apply to what we do with its data. Here's what they add to this Policy.</p>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>Only for your HQ features.</strong> We use platform data only for the HQ features you use. We never use it to train or improve AI models, for ads, or for any other member, and we never sell it. When a feature needs AI, we send Anthropic only what that task needs, and Anthropic doesn't train on it.</li>
<li><strong>No one at 127 reads it</strong> unless you ask us to for help with it, for security, or when the law requires.</li>
<li><strong>We keep it only as long as each platform allows.</strong> Some allow a day or less. What you made from it, like a draft or a plan, stays yours.</li>
<li><strong>Removing access.</strong> Disconnect any platform in HQ, under Connections. We revoke our access there, delete the saved sign-in right away, and delete what HQ got from it within 30 days, apart from what you made from it.</li>
<li><strong>Google.</strong> 127's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. You can also remove 127's access in your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account</a>.</li>
<li><strong>YouTube.</strong> HQ uses YouTube API Services. By connecting YouTube, you agree to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> covers what Google collects. We keep data from YouTube no longer than 30 days unless we refresh it. When you disconnect YouTube in HQ, or remove our access in your Google Account, we stop using it, revoke our access and delete what we got from it within 7 days.</li>
<li><strong>Deleting what HQ got from Facebook or Instagram.</strong> Disconnect Facebook or Instagram in HQ, under Connections, or remove 127 in your Facebook settings under Apps and Websites. We delete the saved sign-in right away and what HQ got from that account within 30 days, apart from what you made from it. You can also email hello@127group.io with the subject &quot;Delete my Facebook data&quot;, and we'll do the same and confirm by email.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="section-8">8. Your rights and choices</h2>
<p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to:</p>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we have about you, and get a portable copy;</li>
<li><strong>Correct</strong> information that's wrong;</li>
<li><strong>Delete</strong> your information;</li>
<li><strong>Opt out</strong> of targeted advertising and any &quot;sale&quot; or &quot;sharing&quot; of your information (use Cookie settings, or a Global Privacy Control signal);</li>
<li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> you've given, such as for marketing emails or ad cookies.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>How to ask.</strong> Delete your account anytime in <strong>Settings → Delete account</strong>. Change your email choice in <strong>Settings</strong>. For anything else, email <strong>hello@127group.io</strong> with the subject &quot;Privacy request.&quot; We'll confirm your request by checking it comes from the email address on file, and we'll respond within 45 days (we'll tell you if we need up to 45 more). You can use an authorized agent; we'll ask for proof of their authority and may verify your identity directly.</p>
<p><strong>Appeals.</strong> If we decline your request, you can appeal by replying to our decision with &quot;Appeal&quot; in the subject. We'll respond within 45 days. If you're unhappy with the outcome, you can contact your state attorney general.</p>
<p>We won't treat you differently for using your privacy rights. Some laws let us keep certain information even after a deletion request, for example records we must keep for taxes, to prevent fraud, or to honor your choice not to receive marketing.</p>
<p><strong>What deletion removes.</strong> Deleting your account cancels any paid subscription immediately and removes your account, assessment answers, progress, worksheets, AI conversations and results, wins posts, Circle application and everything in HQ (Sections 7A and 7B) from our live systems, along with the waitlist, free-tool and Idea Test records linked to your email. We also ask Klaviyo to delete your profile. Stripe keeps payment records as the law requires, and we keep limited billing, consent and agreement records for as long as Section 9 says.</p>
