<h2 id="section-10">10. Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable safeguards for a business of our size: HTTPS everywhere, passwords stored only as salted hashes, payment data held by Stripe, secrets kept out of our code, rate limits and access limited to the people who need it. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal information, we'll notify you as the law requires.</p>
<h2 id="section-11">11. Children</h2>
<p>127 is for people 18 and older. We don't knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe someone under 18 has given us information, email hello@127group.io and we'll delete it. If we learn that a member is under 18, we close the account, refund every payment and delete their information. We keep only a short record that we did so: the dates, the reason, the refund details and a scrambled (one-way hashed) copy of the email address so it can't be used to sign up again, for 3 years. Members who teach or look after children may keep a child's first name, age and lesson notes in HQ for their own work; we hold them only for that member (Section 7B) and never contact the child.</p>
<h2 id="section-12">12. Where we operate</h2>
<p>127 is based in the United States and built for people in the United States. Our service providers process information in the United States and other countries. If you use 127 from outside the United States, your information will be processed in the United States, where laws may differ from those where you live.</p>
<h2 id="section-13">13. State-specific notices</h2>
<ul class="bul">
<li><strong>California (CalOPPA).</strong> This Policy describes the categories of personal information we collect and the categories of third parties we share it with. You can review and request changes as described in Section 8. We treat Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals as described in Section 5. Third parties (Meta and TikTok) can collect information about your online activities over time and across sites only if you accept advertising cookies.</li>
<li><strong>California &quot;Shine the Light.&quot;</strong> We don't share personal information with third parties for their own direct-marketing purposes.</li>
<li><strong>Nevada.</strong> We don't sell covered information as defined by Nevada law. You can still send an opt-out request to hello@127group.io.</li>
<li><strong>Other states.</strong> We're not currently subject to most state comprehensive privacy laws because of our size, but we offer the rights in Section 8 to everyone.</li>
